In the admin list page, when the value of `list_display` is set to '__str__' (default option), if the model's `__str__` is composed entirely of blank values, the link will not appear.
{{{
class Post(models.Model):
    title = models.CharField(max_length=128)
    content = models.TextField()
    like = models.IntegerField(default=0)
    
    def __str__(self):
        return "       "
}}}
[[Image(balnk.png)]]
In a typical situation it would be fine, but when `__str__` is set in `list_display_links`, <a> tag innerHTML becomes empty, so resulting in the loss of the link functionality to navigate to the object.
{{{
class PostAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    list_display_links = ["__str__"]
    list_display = ["__str__", "title"]
}}}
